From: Codex <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] musb: share RTL8723BU HCI interrupt RX endpoint

The first HCI bulk sharing test removed hardware endpoint 5 from the HCI
path, but the Bluetooth interrupt endpoint was still moved from hardware
endpoint 3 to 4 after Wi-Fi initialization and HCI events still stalled.
Route both HCI IN endpoints through the MUSB multiplexed bulk-IN queue.

--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_host.c
@@ -2065,6 +2065,19 @@ static int musb_schedule(
 		hw_ep = musb->control_ep;
 		goto success;
 	}
+
+	if (is_in && musb_qh_is_rtl8723bu(qh) &&
+	    (qh->epnum == 1 || qh->epnum == 2) && musb->bulk_ep) {
+		hw_ep = musb->bulk_ep;
+		head = &musb->in_bulk;
+		if (qh->type == USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_BULK && qh->dev)
+			qh->intv_reg =
+				(USB_SPEED_HIGH == qh->dev->speed) ? 8 : 4;
+		goto success;
+	}
